  "outline": [
    "Built 20 Oct 2026 (Indices clip 7) for skill 3.1 from 108.01 + 108.03 (the notes have no worked example) on a real school question (bank 8006348c, 3 marks): the question read; what we must find (the powers x, y, z); the right side is a power of 2 times a power of 3 times a power of 7, so the plan (shown as maths) is to make the left side the same and compare powers; Negative power flips the fraction ((98/3)^-3 = (3/98)^3, why in a written drop-down); dividing by 7/2 is times 2/7; break every number into the bases 2, 3, 7: 98 = 2 x 49 = 2 x 7^2; In a fraction power the bottom is the root (cube root of 9 = 9^(1/3), why in a written drop-down); Same power: the power 3 goes to every base inside, Times power (7^2)^3 = 7^6; 9 = 3^2, Times power (3^2)^(1/3) = 3^(2/3); every bottom comes UP to the top as a negative power (2^3 and 7^6 move up, then the 7 of 2/7) - the line written with the twos, threes, sevens side by side; Add power on each base: -3 + 1 = -2, 3 + 2/3 = 11/3, -6 + (-1) = -7; same bases, so the powers must be the same: x = -2, y = 11/3, z = -7, boxed. One expression line by line, no step numbers, no Watch out."
  ],
